{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ac8af572df54dcb3","name":"card_unit_7th_brigade_anzac","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/ANZAC/units/card_unit_7th_brigade_anzac","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"7th BRIGADE","text":"Becomes Veteran when your hand is empty. Deployment: Discard your left-most card.","flavorText":"Australia’s 7th Brigade was a Militia formation that played an important role in the Pacific theater during WWII. Initially responsible for defending South East Queensland, it was fully mobilised after Japan entered the war, and by mid-1942 consisted of the 9th, 25th and 61st Battalions. In July 1942, the brigade was sent to Milne Bay in New Guinea, where it fought alongside elements of the 7th Division. In August, Australian forces repelled a Japanese landing aimed at capturing the strategically important Allied airfields, inflicting to Japan its first major defeat on land in the Pacific War. In March 1943, the 7th Brigade was reassigned to the 11th Division and served as part of New Guinea Force’s reserve. It later returned to combat on Bougainville Island, taking part in the battles of Pearl Ridge and Slater’s Knoll.","faction":"Anzac","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_7th_brigade_anzac","title":{"Namespace":"card_anzac","Key":"card_unit_7th_brigade_anzac_title","SourceString":"7th BRIGADE","LocalizedString":"7th BRIGADE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Anzac","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_anzac","Key":"card_unit_7th_brigade_anzac_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran when your hand is empty. Deployment: Discard your left-most card.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran when your hand is empty. Deployment: Discard your left-most card."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_anzac","Key":"card_unit_7th_brigade_anzac_history","SourceString":"Australia’s 7th Brigade was a Militia formation that played an important role in the Pacific theater during WWII. Initially responsible for defending South East Queensland, it was fully mobilised after Japan entered the war, and by mid-1942 consisted of the 9th, 25th and 61st Battalions. In July 1942, the brigade was sent to Milne Bay in New Guinea, where it fought alongside elements of the 7th Division. In August, Australian forces repelled a Japanese landing aimed at capturing the strategically important Allied airfields, inflicting to Japan its first major defeat on land in the Pacific War. In March 1943, the 7th Brigade was reassigned to the 11th Division and served as part of New Guinea Force’s reserve. It later returned to combat on Bougainville Island, taking part in the battles of Pearl Ridge and Slater’s Knoll.","LocalizedString":"Australia’s 7th Brigade was a Militia formation that played an important role in the Pacific theater during WWII. Initially responsible for defending South East Queensland, it was fully mobilised after Japan entered the war, and by mid-1942 consisted of the 9th, 25th and 61st Battalions. In July 1942, the brigade was sent to Milne Bay in New Guinea, where it fought alongside elements of the 7th Division. In August, Australian forces repelled a Japanese landing aimed at capturing the strategically important Allied airfields, inflicting to Japan its first major defeat on land in the Pacific War. In March 1943, the 7th Brigade was reassigned to the 11th Division and served as part of New Guinea Force’s reserve. It later returned to combat on Bougainville Island, taking part in the battles of Pearl Ridge and Slater’s Knoll."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","isInPermanentPool":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDiscarded","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCovertCardPlayedFromHand","ERegistere